Notes (honesty covenant):
  - i18n: every web t() key resolves through the P1/S10 catalogue (translation_theme_{theme,mode,displayMode,
    accentColor,custom,primary,accent}); lifecycle copy via translation_{common_loading,common_retry,common_offline,
    common_noData,error_loadFailed,mqtt_stale,a11y_loading,theme_subtitle}. Brand palette names (Neon Cyan, Dark, ...)
    are catalogue data — exactly as web ThemeProvider holds them as literal name fields, not t() keys.
  - States: loading/content/error/stale/offline are honest (the persisted selection is the surface's async
    dependency, mirroring the web ThemeProvider /settings hydrate). 'empty' is a defensive friendly branch
    (the brand catalogue is static and never empty in production) — rendered + unit-tested, never a blank box.
  - Diagnostics: one-shot view.opened (P1/S11) carries only surface slug 'ThemePicker' — never a theme id or colour.
  - Custom builder: native R/G/B sliders + live swatch + #RRGGBB hex replace the web <input type=color>
    (no Compose system colour input); commits both colours together via setCustomColors (web parity).
  - androidTest source set has PRE-EXISTING, unrelated compile errors in 4 OTHER surfaces (routeplayback,
    scorebadge, scrollrestoration, timelinescrubber) referencing assertExists/onAllNodes; ThemePickerUiTest.kt
    itself compiles cleanly. The gate does not compile/run androidTest (connectedAndroidTest needs a device).

